{"by_variant":{"minimalsanitized":[{"id":"CA1","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[15],"code":"address public handler;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Handler address for bridge deposits. Correctly stored."},{"id":"CA2","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[23],"code":"uint64 public depositNonce;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Deposit nonce for tracking. Correctly implemented."},{"id":"CA3","type":"INITIALIZATION","lines":[25,26,27],"code":"constructor(address _handler) {\n    handler = _handler;\n}\n","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Constructor sets handler. Correctly implemented."},{"id":"CA4","type":"STATE_MOD","lines":[37],"code":"depositNonce += 1;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Nonce increment. Correctly tracks deposits."},{"id":"CA5","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[39],"code":"QBridgeHandler(handler).deposit(resourceID, msg.sender, data);","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Forwards deposit to handler. Correct bridge behavior - the vulnerability is inside the handler."},{"id":"CA6","type":"EVENT_EMIT","lines":[41],"code":"emit Deposit(destinationDomainID, resourceID, depositNonce);","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Event emission. Correctly logs deposit."},{"id":"CA7","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[46],"code":"mapping(bytes32 => address) public resourceIDToTokenContractAddress;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Mapping declaration. The flaw is failure to validate lookup results, not the mapping's existence."},{"id":"CA8","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[47],"code":"mapping(address => bool) public contractWhitelist;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Unused whitelist mapping. Dead state cannot be a prerequisite."},{"id":"CA9","type":"CTRL_FLOW","lines":[57],"code":"address tokenContract = resourceIDToTokenContractAddress[resourceID];","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Mechanical mapping read. The vulnerability is the absence of validation after this read, not the read itself."},{"id":"CA10","type":"COMPUTATION","lines":[62,63],"code":"uint256 amount;\n(amount) = abi.decode(data, (uint256));\n","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Decodes amount from data. Correctly implemented."},{"id":"CA11","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[67],"code":"IERC20(tokenContract).transferFrom(depositer, address(this), amount);","security_function":"ROOT_CAUSE","rationale":"ROOT_CAUSE - Missing validation: tokenContract is used without checking != address(0). For unregistered resourceIDs, this calls address(0) which doesn't revert, allowing deposits without transferring tokens."},{"id":"CA12","type":"ACCESS_CTRL","lines":[76,77,80],"code":"function setResource(bytes32 resourceID, address tokenAddress) external {\n    resourceIDToTokenContractAddress[resourceID] = tokenAddress;\n    // Note: Should also add to whitelist\n}\n","security_function":"SECONDARY_VULN","rationale":"SECONDARY_VULN - setResource has no access control. Anyone can set resource mappings. However, main vulnerability is that deposit doesn't validate tokenContract != address(0)."},{"id":"CA_DIRECTIVES","type":"DIRECTIVE","lines":[1,2],"security_function":"UNRELATED","rationale":"License and pragma statements"},{"id":"CA_COMMENTS","type":"COMMENT","lines":[29,30,31,49,50,51,59,60,65,66,69,70,73,74,75,79],"security_function":"UNRELATED","rationale":"Inline comments and NatSpec documentation"},{"id":"CA_DECLARATIONS","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12,14,17,18,19,20,21,32,33,34,35,36,43,45,52,53,54,55,56,71,80,81],"security_function":"UNRELATED","rationale":"Interface, contract, event, and function signature declarations"},{"id":"CA_SYNTAX","type":"SYNTAX","lines":[42,68],"security_function":"UNRELATED","rationale":"Closing braces"}],"differential":[{"id":"CA_FIX1","type":"INPUT_VAL","lines":[52],"code":"require(tokenContract != address(0), \"Invalid token\");","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"FIX - Validates tokenContract is not zero address before attempting transfer."},{"id":"CA_FIX2","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[57,58],"code":"bool success = IERC20(tokenContract).transferFrom(depositer, address(this), amount);\nrequire(success, \"Transfer failed\");\n","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"FIX - Checks transfer return value to ensure deposit succeeded."},{"id":"CA_FIX3","type":"INPUT_VAL","lines":[62],"code":"require(tokenAddress != address(0), \"Invalid token\");","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"FIX - Prevents setting zero address as resource token."},{"id":"CA1","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[15],"code":"address public handler;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Handler address."},{"id":"CA2","type":"STATE_MOD","lines":[34],"code":"depositNonce += 1;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Nonce increment."},{"id":"CA3","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[36],"code":"BridgeHandler(handler).deposit(resourceID, msg.sender, data);","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Deposit forwarding."},{"id":"CA4","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[43,44],"code":"mapping(bytes32 => address) public resourceIDToTokenContractAddress;\nmapping(address => bool) public contractWhitelist;\n","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Handler state variables."},{"id":"CA5","type":"CTRL_FLOW","lines":[51],"code":"address tokenContract = resourceIDToTokenContractAddress[resourceID];","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Token address lookup."},{"id":"CA6","type":"COMPUTATION","lines":[54,55],"code":"uint256 amount;\n(amount) = abi.decode(data, (uint256));\n","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Amount decoding."},{"id":"CA7","type":"STATE_MOD","lines":[63],"code":"resourceIDToTokenContractAddress[resourceID] = tokenAddress;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Resource mapping update. Now protected by zero address check."},{"id":"CA_DIRECTIVES","type":"DIRECTIVE","lines":[1,2],"security_function":"UNRELATED","rationale":"License and pragma statements"},{"id":"CA_DECLARATIONS","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12,14,17,18,19,20,21,23,25,26,27,29,30,31,32,33,38,39,40,42,46,47,48,49,50,59,61,64,65],"security_function":"UNRELATED","rationale":"Interface, contract, event, and function signature declarations"},{"id":"CA_SYNTAX","type":"SYNTAX","lines":[13,60],"security_function":"UNRELATED","rationale":"Closing braces"}],"trojan":[{"id":"CA_ROOT1","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[93],"security_function":"ROOT_CAUSE","rationale":"ROOT_CAUSE - transferFrom called on tokenContract which may be address(0)."},{"id":"INJ1","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[71,72,73],"security_function":"DECOY","rationale":"DECOY - Suspicious variable names look like vulnerabilities but are benign."},{"id":"INJ2","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[76,77],"security_function":"DECOY","rationale":"DECOY - Analytics variables with suspicious names."},{"id":"INJ3","type":"CTRL_FLOW","lines":[89,90,91],"security_function":"DECOY","rationale":"DECOY - Zero address check looks protective but doesn't prevent the vulnerability."},{"id":"INJ4","type":"CTRL_FLOW","lines":[95,96,97],"security_function":"DECOY","rationale":"DECOY - Bypass check looks dangerous but just updates counter."},{"id":"INJ5","type":"CTRL_FLOW","lines":[103,104],"security_function":"DECOY","rationale":"DECOY - Emergency override looks dangerous but emergencyTokenOverride is unused."},{"id":"INJ6","type":"ACCESS_CTRL","lines":[109,110,111,112],"security_function":"DECOY","rationale":"DECOY - Unprotected toggle looks dangerous but bypass only affects analytics."},{"id":"INJ7","type":"COMPUTATION","lines":[115,116,117,118,119,120,121],"security_function":"DECOY","rationale":"DECOY - View function is safe."},{"id":"INJ8","type":"COMPUTATION","lines":[123,124,125,126,127,128,129,130,131,132,133],"security_function":"DECOY","rationale":"DECOY - View function is safe."},{"id":"CA1","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[67,68],"security_function":"PREREQ","rationale":"PREREQ - Resource mapping that may not be initialized."},{"id":"CA2","type":"STATE_MOD","lines":[84],"security_function":"BENI